# Minimal liberty technology-mapping recipe for ABC, used by
# synth_pe_mixed_abcfix.tcl in place of Yosys's default abc script.
#
# The default Yosys `abc -liberty` recipe runs:
#   strash; &get -n; &fraig -x; &put; scorr; dc2; dretime; strash;
#   &get -n; &dch -f; &nf; &put; write_blif
#
# scorr/dc2/dretime/&dch/&nf are sequential-equivalence / choice-based
# resynthesis passes. pe_int8 goes through that exact recipe cleanly on both
# sky130 and FreePDK45; pe_mixed does not (49 "wire has no driver" problems
# on a_out/b_out/valid_out/acc_q - see logs/synth_pe_mixed_sky130_20261016.log
# and ../asic/logs/synth_pe_mixed_freepdk45.log for the full analysis).
# Working theory: a scale-triggered re-integration defect in those extra
# passes, not an RTL bug (cocotb passes on pe_mixed's RTL in both
# ENABLE_GATING settings). This script strips the recipe down to bare
# structural hashing + direct liberty mapping, with no sequential-equivalence
# or choice-based passes, to test that theory in isolation.
strash
map
